{#-
  The qyl-owned instruments: one `public static class {Root}MetricAttributes` per registry root
  that owns one, carrying each instrument's name and its unit as `const string`.

  Only rows the registry attributes to qyl are projected. An upstream instrument belongs to
  OpenTelemetry and reaches a consumer as a MetricDefinition; a qyl-owned instrument is qyl's
  own vocabulary, and the components that create it — the collector included — must not spell
  it as a literal. The class name ends in `Attributes` and sits under `.Attributes.` because
  the qyl collector may not reference this package family and builds its vocabulary by
  reflecting over exactly those types' `const string` members.
-#}
